<title>USA: ConAgra Q4 May 25 profit vs loss. [CORRECTED 15:20 GMT]</title>
<headline>ConAgra Q4 May 25 profit vs loss. [CORRECTED 15:20 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>OMAHA, Neb. 1997-07-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p>(Corrects time period in column heading).</p>
<p> Shr	 profit	 $0.81     loss	 $0.84</p>
<p> Net	 profit     186,500     loss     193,700</p>
<p> Revs		   5,795,300		5,747,200</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 229,600		  230,600</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Year-ago Q4 after non-recurring restructuring and related charges of $356.3 million or $1.55 after tax. Excluding charge, Q4 1996 net income $162.6 million or $0.71 a share.  </p>
<p>		     YEAR</p>
<p> Shr   profit	     $2.68   profit	 $0.79</p>
<p> Net   profit	   615,000   profit     188,900</p>
<p> Revs		  24,002,100	     23,899,300</p>
<p> Avg shrs		 229,500		  229,500</p>
<p>(Corrects 1996 year revenues to 23,899,300 from 2,899,300).</p>
<p>(All Data Above 000s Except Per Share Numbers)</p>
<p>NOTE: Year-ago net income before $8.6 million in preferred dividends.</p>
<p>Year-ago net income after $356.3 million or $1.55 a share charge. Excluding charge, fiscal 1996 income was $545.2 million with net income available to common stock of $536.6 million and earnings per share of $2.34.</p>
<p>ConAgra Inc.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
